+# Agent Note: Readonly trajectory inspection
+
+Status: implemented
+
+English | [中文](2026-09-18-trajectory-inspection.zh.md)
+
+## Problem
+
+A plugin can need to inspect history outside the active path or display a saved request in a different order. Changing Session history for inspection affects execution; copying the trajectory renderer loses shared detail and attachment behavior.
+
+## Decision
+
+Trajectory owns an effect-scoped readonly source registry and navigation slots. Conversation assembles explicit event windows using its existing definitions. Ordered context records retain original message identities and source links independently of presentation indexes. Execution records retain turn, step and request grouping. Context references have no new timing or usage. A provider can identify durable user inputs for presentation, preserving their original producer metadata. This keeps replayed user actions distinct from injected instructions without rewriting source events.
+
+## Alternatives considered
+
+Mutating the active Conversation binding couples inspection to Chat and execution. Fabricating event sequence numbers or timestamps hides source identity. A separate text-only renderer duplicates presentation policy and drops tool and request inspection.
+
+## Consequences
+
+Registration disposal restores the ordinary source. Plugins supply selection semantics, translated labels and immutable request reads; the generic ledger supplies its existing search, fold, detail and copy behavior. No Session event or SDK format changes. Tests cover reordered references, ordinary views, built bundles and effect cleanup. The [package reference](../../../../packages/client/ui-trajectory/README.md) owns the public extension contract.
